  "caption_latex": "Isolated spin--cavity feedback control. {(a,b):} Mixed covariance magnitude $|\\langle\\sigma^y p\\rangle_c|$, with $p=(a-a^\\dagger)/(i\\sqrt{2})$, for number-loss rates $\\kappa/\\omega_c=0.2$ and $0.52$, respectively. {(c,d):} Spin--cavity entanglement negativity for the same two loss rates. Each panel compares feedback off (purple), feedback on (orange) and independent drive noise (teal); matching observables share a vertical scale. The local Rabi parameters, vacuum/ground preparation, gain $f=0.15\\sqrt{\\omega_c}$ and phase $\\pi/2$ match the chain. Independent noise does not reproduce the feedback-assisted persistence. Solid photon-cap-eight master equations overlap the dotted cap-five checks: maximum changes are $3.1\\times10^{-6}$ in mixed correlations and $9.3\\times10^{-7}$ in negativity. These deterministic controls are not HOPS."
